if(req.method==="GET"&&path==="/privacy")return plain('<main style="max-width:800px;margin:auto;padding:30px;font:16px/1.65 system-ui"><h1>REMAKE by objekts — Privacy</h1><p>REMAKE provides stateless tools supporting a host-led creative and production audit from objekts; the server has no inference model. Most MCP tools operate only on user-supplied text descriptors, project state, shot notes, source references and LOCKs. An optional ChatGPT file preflight tool may fetch an explicitly selected image/video file temporarily to calculate its SHA256 and file metadata (maximum 12 MiB per request). The <code>remake_host_image_for_review</code> and <code>remake_host_image_batch</code> tools may temporarily fetch explicitly selected PNG/JPEG images and return their actual pixels to the requesting AI host as separate MCP image content blocks (up to 2 MiB per image; batches up to 8 images and 8 MiB aggregate; further calls can handle additional project sources). Every file retains its source reference and SHA256. The server does not use a visual AI model to analyze those pixels; the AI host may process or retain returned images according to its own privacy policy.</p><p><b>Storage and sharing.</b> This service processes file bytes only transiently in Worker memory; it does not intentionally save raw files to the REMAKE application database, forward files to objekts producers, sell source materials or automatically create sales enquiries. Source SHA256, dimensions and basic metadata are returned to the calling client. Cloudflare may process technical traffic and security metadata under its platform policies; the AI host may separately retain the content it receives. No project accounts or long-term cross-session storage are provided through the public MCP.</p><p><b>Static studio image.</b> The REMAKE-generated landing HTML references a public studio icon from raw.githubusercontent.com. Your browser contacts that external static host and may disclose standard network/request metadata under its policies; no project or private media is included. The page and image use no-referrer policy. REMAKE generates no project upload fields, forms or application scripts.</p><p><b>Cloudflare delivery.</b> Cloudflare adds a WebMCP bridge at <code>/.webmcp/bridge.js</code> when delivering HTML; the current delivered tag selects only the Content Credentials (C2PA) pack (<code>data-packs=c2pa</code>). Where supported and permitted by browser policy, this pack can fetch images and read provenance metadata locally in the browser. Image hosts may receive normal network/request metadata. Reading credentials does not verify their cryptographic signatures. A delivered tag does not establish that it executed in your browser. This delivery component is separate from REMAKE-generated HTML and MCP file tools. See <a href="https://blog.cloudflare.com/webmcp/">Cloudflare documentation</a>.</p><p><b>Control.</b> File analysis occurs only after the calling client supplies a selected file reference. Do not provide sensitive or third-party confidential materials without the appropriate rights and permission. For questions about data handling, rights or technical support, contact <a href="mailto:salute@objekts.ai">salute@objekts.ai</a>. Publisher: <a href="https://objekts.ai/">objekts</a>.</p></main>');
